fix(runtime): probe .NET without spawning a child process

Docs amended: the previous commit claimed this fix while the code still
had it -- the working-tree change was lost by a `git checkout -- .` during
an unrelated bisect rollback, and nobody re-checked.

is_dotnet_installed() ran `dotnet --list-runtimes` through
std::process::Command::output(). Creating a process on Windows briefly
blocks every thread in the parent (the loader holds a process-wide lock),
and that stall lands in the window's first-paint window -- the translucent
rectangle seen at launch. spawn_blocking does not help, because the stall
is in process creation itself.

Probe the well-known install roots on disk instead: a few read_dir calls,
no child process.